{
 "_doc": [
  "Merged bindings: one native file per installed directory set, exporting every member's PyInit.",
  "Each member keeps its module name; python/mojolearn/_merged.py loads it from the merged file",
  "through the directory's _mojolearn_merged.json index when its own .so is absent.",
  "dirs.<dir>.groups: merged file stem -> members. Adding a binding is one line in its group.",
  "A directory holds SEVERAL groups: each group is one `mojo build`, and one compile's peak RSS grows with",
  "its members (the single 46-member host compile passed 40 GB in 0.8.59 and paged for 5700 s on a 16 GB",
  "GitHub runner). Groups are balanced by the members' measured peaks (per-member development builds,",
  "~/mojolearn-evidence/dev-cache-mac/peaks, 2026-10-26) so each compile fits a 16 GB runner; the heavy",
  "members (tokenizer, neural, byte LM, forest) sit in different groups. A stem never equals a member,",
  "and every host stem ends in _host so the packers' _mojolearn_*_host.so glob still finds it.",
  "Splitting changes link units only: same sources, same flags, same kernels, no bit change.",
  "dirs.<dir>.optional: member -> {group, platforms}: it joins that group on those platforms when MOJOLEARN_PACKAGE_BYTE_LM=1.",
  "darwin_metal1: members whose per-binding script passes --target-accelerator metal:1 on macOS;",
  "on macOS they compile into <stem>_m1 so every member keeps its own compile flags.",
  "tools/merged_bindings.py reads this file; bindings/merged_build.sh builds it."
 ],
